ngles of Burma or on the D-Day beaches, as submariners, pilots, spies or prisoners of war, young soldiers in WWII displayed astonishing courage and resilience, united by honour and bound by the fellowship of their comrades. Those who made it home are now a passing generation, and for many this is th\n\nBook 2:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007214686\n  Title: Shaman\'s Crossing\n  Categories: Unknown\n  Description: The first book in a brand new trilogy from the author of the Farseer, Liveship Traders and Tawny Man trilogies.\n\nBook 3:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007218011\n  Title: The Last Kingdom\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: The first book in the epic and bestselling series that has gripped millions. A hero will be forged from this broken land. As seen on Netflix and BBC around the world. In a land torn apart by conflict, an orphan boy has come of age. Raised by the Vikings, deadly enemies of his own Saxon people, Uhtred is a fierce and skilled warrior who kneels to no-one. Alfred - Saxon, king, man of god - fights to hold the throne of the only land still resisting the pagan northerners. Uhtred and Alfred\'s fates are tangled, soaked in blood and blackened by the flames of war. Together they will change history.\n\nBook 4:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007231386\n  Title: Slawter\n  Categories: Juvenile Nonfiction\n  Description: While on a horror movie set with his Uncle Dervish, Grubbs Grady realizes that his battle with the evil demon master Lord Loss may be about to resume.\n\nBook 5:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007260454\n  Title: Dark Calling\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: Events take an unexpected turn in this ninth awesome foray into the worlds of the Demonata... Suitable for ages 10+ "I know it\'s ridiculous. Lights can\'t whisper. But I swear I heard a voice calling to me. It sounded like static to begin with, but then it came into focus, a single word repeated over and over. Softly, slyly, seductively, insistently. Come..." the Disciples are being manipulated by beings older than time. Only Kernel Fleck knows that something is wrong. But he is in the grip of a creature who cares nothing for the fate of humanity. Voices are calling to him from the darkness and\n\nBook 6:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007267545\n  Title: Odd Hours\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: The latest Odd Thomas thriller from the master storyteller. A mystery in Magic Beach, California has lured Odd to the small town by the ocean -- but is it the call of the deep or the cry of the desperate?\n\nBook 7:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007267576\n  Title: Your Heart Belongs to Me\n  Categories: Heart\n  Description: At 34 Ryan Perry suddenly finds himself on a waiting list for a heart transplant. Although he keeps working and looks fit, his condition is deteriorating. He\'s in an ever-tighter medical corner, and his girlfriend Samantha, who had been so supportive, suddenly can\'t take the pressure; she leaves. Nevertheless, Ryan manages to remain upbeat, and his reward is well deserved. He receives a new heart, and the transplant is a success. One year later, Ryan has never felt better. He is dealing well with business problems, even with the mystery of Samantha\'s continuing coolness. Life is good, very goo\n\nBook 8:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007274444\n  Title: Brida\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: The spellbinding new novel from one of the world\'s best-loved authors, Paulo Coelho, recounting the story of Brida, and her pursuit of wisdom.\n\nBook 9:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007281800\n  Title: The Pocket Dangerous Book for Boys\n  Categories: Natural history\n  Description: Continuing the momentum of "The Dangerous Book for Boys" phenomenon, this pocket-sized reference guide is filled with endless hours of hands-on activities that boys will want to take everywhere.\n\nBook 10:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007290277\n  Title: The Inheritance\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: A collection of novellas and stories from one of the most critically acclaimed authors in the fantasy genre, Robin Hobb. Including work written under her pseudonym, Megan Lindholm.\n\n\nRemember:\n- Vary query length (short / medium / long)\n- Do not repeat the book title\n- Focus on themes, emotions, plot, and characters\n', 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'$defs': {'BookQueries': {'description': 'Structured output for queries generated for a single book.\n\nThe LLM is asked to produce queries of varying lengths to simulate\ndifferent user search behaviours.', 'properties': {'isbn13': {'description': 'ISBN-13 of the source book these queries were generated for.', 'title': 'Isbn13', 'type': 'string'}, 'queries': {'description': 'List of search queries relevant to the book. Should include short (1-3 words), medium (4-8 words), and long (9+ words) queries.', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'title': 'Queries', 'type': 'array'}}, 'required': ['isbn13', 'queries'], 'title': 'BookQueries', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}}, 'description': 'Structured output returned by the LLM for a batch of books.\n\nWrapping in a single batch call reduces API round-trips and token overhead.', 'properties': {'books': {'description': 'One BookQueries entry per book in the input batch.', 'items': {'$ref': '#/$defs/BookQueries'}, 'title': 'Books', 'type': 'array'}}, 'required': ['books'], 'title': 'BatchQueryResponse', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}, 'name': 'BatchQueryResponse', 'strict': True}}, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.0}}
