2026-06-10 15:53:06 | DEBUG    | openai._base_client | Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Helper-Method': 'chat.completions.parse', 'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a0549a22-2262-4d9d-86c1-e00a4eeabf3f', 'post_parser': <function Completions.parse.<locals>.parser at 0x000001F15F35F100>, 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': 'You are an expert book search query generator for an information retrieval benchmark.\n\nYour task is to generate realistic search queries that a user might type into a book search engine.\n\nFor EACH book in the list:\n1. Generate exactly 2 queries\n2. Queries must vary in length:\n   - At least 1 SHORT query (1–4 words, e.g., "dragon fantasy adventure")\n   - At least 1 MEDIUM query (5–10 words, e.g., "coming of age story in a small southern town")\n   - At least 1 LONG query (11+ words, e.g., "psychological thriller where the protagonist cannot trust her own memory after a traumatic accident")\n3. DO NOT repeat or closely paraphrase the book title\n4. Focus on: themes, plot elements, characters, emotional tone, setting, topics\n5. Make queries feel like genuine user searches – not descriptions of the book\n\nReturn a JSON object matching the BatchQueryResponse schema with one entry per book.\nThe `isbn13` field in each BookQueries entry must match the isbn13 from the input.\n', 'role': 'system'}, {'content': "Generate 2 search queries for each of the following 10 book(s):\n\nBook 1:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007346295\n  Title: Coco Chanel: The Legend and the Life\n  Categories: Biography & Autobiography\n  Description: Justine Picardie has spent the last decade puzzling over the truth about Coco Chanel, attempting to peel away the accretions of romance and lies. In this critically acclaimed, bestselling biography she shares the history of the incredible woman who created the way we look now.\n\nBook 2:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007353132\n  Title: Blow by Blow\n  Categories: Celebrities\n  Description: Isabella Blow was the epitome of English eccentricity. A legendary figure in the fashion world, she nurtured and championed the talent of some of fashion's most recognisable and important figures, all the time hiding her own personal unhappiness and severe depression. This is her story, told by her husband, Detmar.\n\nBook 3:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007353989\n  Title: Lost Souls (Dean Koontz’s Frankenstein, Book 4)\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: SOMEONE NEW IS PLAYING GOD The Frankenstein story updated to the 21st century by the great American storyteller Dean Koontz.\n\nBook 4:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007354733\n  Title: Destination Unknown\n  Categories: Conspiracy\n  Description: When a number of leading scientists disappear without trace, concern grows within the intelligence services. Are they being kidnapped? Blackmailed? One woman appears to hold the key to the mystery. Unfortunately, Olive Betterton now lies dying from injuries sustained in a Moroccan plane crash.\n\nBook 5:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007355259\n  Title: Abarat 2: Days of Magic, Nights of War\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: A dazzling fantasy adventure for all ages, the second part of a quartet appearing at two yearly intervals, richly illustrated by the author. Film rights sold to Disney for $8 million on the paintings alone.\n\nBook 6:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007355563\n  Title: Galilee\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: A massive tale of secrets, corruption and magic between two feuding families the powerful Gearys and the shadowy Barbarossas.\n\nBook 7:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007369683\n  Title: Looking For Alaska\n  Categories: Young Adult Fiction\n  Description: The unmissable first novel from bestselling and award-winning author of THE FAULT IN OUR STARS and TURTLES ALL THE WAY DOWN.\n\nBook 8:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007375394\n  Title: Prodigal Son (Dean Koontz’s Frankenstein, Book 1)\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: SOMEONE NEW IS PLAYING GOD The Frankenstein story updated to the 21st century by the great American storyteller Dean Koontz.\n\nBook 9:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007375400\n  Title: City of Night (Dean Koontz’s Frankenstein, Book 2)\n  Categories: Fiction\n  Description: The Frankenstein story is updated to the 21st century by the great American storyteller Dean Koontz. Now someone new is playing god.\n\nBook 10:\n  ISBN-13: 9780007379620\n  Title: The Thing Around Your Neck\n  Categories: Unknown\n  Description: A collection of twelve stories includes the tale of a medical student in hiding with a poor Muslim woman, and a woman who discovers a devastating secret about her brother's death.\n\n\nRemember:\n- Vary query length (short / medium / long)\n- Do not repeat the book title\n- Focus on themes, emotions, plot, and characters\n", 'role': 'user'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o-mini', 'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'schema': {'$defs': {'BookQueries': {'description': 'Structured output for queries generated for a single book.\n\nThe LLM is asked to produce queries of varying lengths to simulate\ndifferent user search behaviours.', 'properties': {'isbn13': {'description': 'ISBN-13 of the source book these queries were generated for.', 'title': 'Isbn13', 'type': 'string'}, 'queries': {'description': 'List of search queries relevant to the book. Should include short (1-3 words), medium (4-8 words), and long (9+ words) queries.', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'title': 'Queries', 'type': 'array'}}, 'required': ['isbn13', 'queries'], 'title': 'BookQueries', 'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False}}, 'description': 'Structured output returned by the LLM for a batch of books.\n\nWrapping in a single batch call reduces API round-trips and token overhead.', 'properties': {'books': {'description': 'One BookQueries entry per book in the input batch.', 'items': {'$ref': '#/$defs/BookQueries'}, 'title': 'Books', 'type': 'array'}}, 'required': ['bo